# BJT Deck & Flashcard Management Skill

Use this skill when implementing, reviewing, or polishing Deck / Flashcard management features for the Nihongo BJT mobile app.

## Goal

Implement mobile Deck and Flashcard management with full parity to the web app where appropriate, while keeping the UX mobile-native, production-grade, and suitable for Japanese/Vietnamese learning.

This includes:
- deck list
- deck detail
- create deck
- edit deck
- delete/archive deck
- flashcard list inside deck
- create flashcard
- edit flashcard
- delete/archive flashcard
- search/filter/sort
- import/export if web supports it
- saved/review/SRS integration
- empty/loading/error/offline states
- Japanese/Vietnamese typography
- widget/integration tests

## Hard rules

- Do not fake deck or flashcard data.
- Do not invent API responses.
- Do not mark a web feature as deferred unless the API/client/model was searched and the blocker is documented.
- Reuse existing web API contracts when available.
- Reuse existing mobile repositories/providers/patterns.
- Do not modify backend/API/database unless explicitly required.
- Do not break Review/SRS flow.
- Do not break existing Flashcard reveal behavior.
- Keep Review tab active for flashcard/deck flows launched from Review.
- Do not show bottom navigation on focused review/practice flows if it interferes with CTA/touch behavior.
- Add/update tests for every management action.
- Keep Vietnamese and Japanese localization in sync.
- Do not claim device QA passed unless actually tested.

